<BaseLayout title="Research | Artem Kachan" description="Research and applied product work by Artem Kachan."><main class="page section"><a class="text-link" href="/">← Home</a><div class="section-heading" style="margin-top:4rem"><div class="eyebrow">Research</div><h1 class="case-title">Research that informs the product.</h1></div><div class="case-content"><section><h2>Academic research</h2><p>Developed and publicly defended three prize-winning Junior Academy of Sciences research projects, including ancient shipbuilding translated into 3D models and physical experiments, and analysis of disinformation methods in mass media.</p></section><section><h2>Reasoning diagnosis</h2><p>ReTrace explores how learning software can locate the earliest invalid reasoning step rather than immediately supplying an answer.</p></section><section><h2>Local-first educational systems</h2><p>TutPro explores reliable educational operations, offline persistence, synchronization, ownership boundaries, and multi-user educational data.</p></section><section><h2>Mathematical experiments</h2><p>Cyclic Sequence Analyser applies DFT to periodic numerical sequences and expresses detected patterns through trigonometric equations.</p></section></div></main></BaseLayout>
